{"kind":"request","text":"Rollout configuration for the security union (main f7b59bf9) on the hosted Workers.\n\nMain f7b59bf9 cannot go to artroom-scope, dap-grow or dap-lending with the configurations as they are:\n\n- SCOPE_INDEX_MODE is not set, and it defaults to enforce. An enforce deploy before the sweep refuses every scope that is not in the index.\n- APPLICATION_SCREEN_HOSTS is not set, and an empty mapping refuses. The grow and lending application screens stop.\n- dap-application-sandbox has SCREEN_HOSTS [] and is not deployed.\n\nAsked: one reviewed head with the nonsecret configuration that the planner deploys.\n\n1. For each room Worker (artroom-scope, dap-grow, dap-lending): its APPLICATION_SCREEN_HOSTS descriptors, with one screen host under inguz.space for each installed application that has screens. Name each host.\n2. The matching SCREEN_HOSTS for dap-application-sandbox.\n3. A way to deploy with SCOPE_INDEX_MODE=register for steps 2 and 3 of the scope index rollout, and with enforce for step 4, with no edit to a checked-in file between the steps (for example a --var at deploy time, written in the runbook).\n4. A short ordered runbook in notes/implementation/2026-10-22-security-union.md: the order of the Worker deploys, the DNS and route needs for *.inguz.space (the zone and its wildcard record exist), the check after each deploy, and the rollback version to record.\n5. Say whether the Counter and Lending screens need new signed releases before they work under R8. If they do, file a separate request for each.\n\nThe planner has the step 1 inventories against the pre-index deployments: dap-grow 11 scopes (manifest sha256 902ac75bc1867a5dac649d2bf7b5e25b6ee8aeab83c2fa0fce92b25aa8e698a8) and dap-lending 8 scopes (cd67ae0a15d129f93672827df6b618ccfed1d479899eb3990598e119fa5dbe8e). artroom-scope needs its list of known rooms first.\n\nKernel placement: work on existing forms. It adds no scope kind, definition name, capability, tool family or record model.","body":{"conditions":"Configuration and runbook text only; no code change. One gate at the head; checker review at the exact head before landing. No deployment by the builder. Plain English per ISO 24495-1.","priority":"after the archive pass diagnostic (03c284f5); ahead of K9 (2e714fd7) and the rename (5c54039c)","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}